3.2. Implementation in ABAQUS
The solution is implemented in ABAQUS by using its user subroutines UEL and USDFLD. Two element types, which share the same nodes but contain different degrees of freedom (DOFs), are used in a layered manner [43,47]. The first type of element is coupled with the DOFs of displacement and temperature. The second type of element has only one DOF to calculate the phase field. The phase-field damage variable d is set as a field variable in the user subroutine USDFLD, which can change the material properties at the Gauss integration points during the calculation. As a result, the effects of the phase-field damage variable d on the mechanical and thermal properties can be easily implemented. In 3D simulations, the user subroutine UFILM is used to consider the effects of the water entry posture on thermal shock-induced cracking behaviors under prescribed thermal boundary conditions.
